# The golden fixture is a COMMITTED database on purpose — it is FR-D1's binding,
# the only test that migrates real data rather than empty tables. Without this
# exception `*.db` above silently excludes it, and the gate passes locally while
# being absent from CI, which is the worst of both.
# Rebuild deliberately: node scripts/make-golden-fixture.mjs
!tests/fixtures/*.db
.agents/
.env
.env.*
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
.venv/
*.tgz
package.json.prepack-backup

# Generated by `npm run test:coverage`. Was tracked (105 files, last refreshed
# 2026-03-04) until 2026-08-07: the committed HTML reported 29.54%/21.15% against
# a real 35.54%/25.55%, and running the command dirtied 103 tracked files, so the
# only way to measure coverage was to make the tree look modified. Senior review S11.
coverage/
